HTTP/REST request tool with two project-specific extensions a stock HTTP client doesn't have:

1. **Pod-aware auth.** Any header value, OR any string field inside a JSON-encoded `body`, that starts with `datapod:<kind>:<id>[/<projection>]` resolves at courier scope at execute time — the secret bytes never enter your transcript. Per-field substitution recurses into nested objects and arrays. Example for Bluesky createSession:

```
body: "{\"identifier\":\"<handle>\",\"password\":\"datapod:auth.bearer:<id>/full\"}"
```

2. **Pod-sealed response.** Set `response_pod_kind` (e.g. `'health.private'`, `'financial.private'`) to seal the response body into a new pod at that privacy class. The agent gets `response_pod_id` instead of body content; downstream skills at the appropriate authority `pod_fetch` to act on it.

`body` is ALWAYS a string. For JSON APIs, JSON-encode and pass; the tool `json.loads` at execute time. `expect_status` (e.g. `[200]`) fails the call loudly on any other status; omit it to let the agent inspect the status itself.

NOT for: browser-rendered pages or interactive logins → `playwright_manager`. Static page reads → `scrape_url`. Calling another agent / running a routine → invoke that manager directly.
